    <node id="scurvy_harpooner">
      <data key="d0">scurvy_harpooner</data>
      <data key="d1">user</data>
      <data key="d2">Scurvy_Harpooner is an active community member and player involved in discussions and gameplay related to the game Crown of Brine. They advocate for the establishment of a dedicated glitchless category within the game to promote authentic gameplay and ensure fair competition among players. This highlights their commitment to maintaining the integrity and challenge of the game experience.

As a knowledgeable contributor, Scurvy_Harpooner provides practical advice on gameplay techniques, emphasizing the importance of rhythm, timing, and patience, particularly in mastering specific challenges such as the parrot’s whistle and spectral strikes. They advise players to avoid rapid button mashing and instead focus on precise timing intervals and environmental control to improve success rates. Their insights also include guidance on reading tide markers and aligning flash times with tide charts to accurately decode in-game puzzles like the Lighthouse Cipher, reflecting a deep understanding of game mechanics.

Beyond gameplay, Scurvy_Harpooner engages in community support by reminding members about proper tagging conventions, including the use of solved, duplicate, and remaster tags, to enhance forum clarity and organization. This contribution demonstrates their role in fostering a well-structured and accessible knowledge-sharing environment.

Scurvy_Harpooner also reports technical issues encountered while playing the game across different platforms. They have experienced save corruption problems on both Linux and iOS devices, notably after decoding the salt-bone amulet on an iPhone. To mitigate the issue on Linux, they share a temporary workaround involving the disabling of voice-acting. Additionally, they address softlock bugs by recommending players check sound settings and follow walkthrough steps to prevent or recover from the problem.

Overall, Scurvy_Harpooner exemplifies an engaged and supportive member of the Crown of Brine community, contributing strategic gameplay advice, advocating for fair and glitch-free categories, assisting with technical troubleshooting, and promoting effective community organization.&lt;SEP&gt;Scurvy_Harpooner is a community member who praises the embroidered spectral cutlass for its intricate details and blend of classic and fresh design elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Scurvy_Harpooner is a community member who commented on the fan-art, appreciating the eerie solitude and thematic elements such as cryptic symbols and the modded environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Scurvy_Harpooner is a player character who explains detailed strategies involving patrol timing, item collection, vent navigation, and hacking a control panel to escape the brig in game-1.&lt;SEP&gt;Scurvy_Harpooner is a user reporting and discussing the audio dropout issue experienced in the modded version of Forgotten Lighthouse on C64, sharing observations and potential fixes.&lt;SEP&gt;Forum user: scurvy_harpooner</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8cb40b7b88f8ddedfd10a5ec14d2e48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e49542a2243a39d767cd5cd1f624d09c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17db7f1fd3181db65c0602e11860133e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e47864ec6178c41b815896a4f5c6acf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9dca83ba0205d167887ed3c0fc9f7ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a13678402573cc3e73bc43b3ea412ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e3000b4af96c385d975af2e2b636806&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c30b0ebef9a74782bd6344e4c1f04ec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4f4af8e72c04a161f49d743827f2491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-976b0b38affc91ce64e175128337fad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7787d1295d99122e8d6b0ddde291fddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fef00793a255df2a6503deabcb8f95a</data>
